.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Use published OGOs as a year-round source of truth for which aspirational values are being lived—
    so annual values awards can be chosen from leaderboards, not only end-of-year nominations.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    Aspirational values are rated on OGOs. Kudos points linked to those observations feed champion scores.
    Values check-ins use the same employee / manager / final clarity pattern as assignment check-ins.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-0
    %li
      %strong Which values are we living?
      ranks unarchived values by OGO volume in the selected timeframe. Totals include private OGOs; journals are excluded.
    %li
      %strong Champions
      show top 10 observees and top 10 observers per value from
      %em public
      OGOs only, sorted by OGO count then points. Private-only activity never places someone on the public board.
    %li
      %strong Clarity
      plots the latest finalized values check-in per person × value. Use Dots / Names to switch marker style.
      Dots always redact. Names shows people you can see: all teammates if you have manage employment,
      otherwise only yourself and people in your managerial hierarchy.
